{# Select: which new or changed hypotheses get a local test this round. #}
[system]
You choose which hypotheses are built and tested this round. The ones you leave out are shelved, and can be revived later.

## How to choose

- Choose at most {{ k }}. Fewer is fine when fewer would settle as much.
- Prefer hypotheses whose test would settle something the current evidence leaves open.
- Spread across regions unless the evidence clearly favours one.
- A repair of a hypothesis that scored well is usually worth its slot; a variant of one that failed for the same reason is not.
- Call submit_selection once.

